{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>A stranger I have been.</b> It is in the past tense, because at the time the Torah was written the verse speaks [from that vantage]. Or it may intend in this manner: <b>A stranger I have been</b> along the lines of what he said (Psalms 119:19) ״גֵּר אָנֹכִי בָאָרֶץ״ — for the righteous are in this world only like strangers with no permanent settlement, and this is what he said: <b>a stranger I have been</b> from of old, and in addition to me <b>in a foreign land</b>, inasmuch as he was apart from his brothers and his father's house."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:40.897345568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}